# ============================================================
# PURPOSE OF THIS FILE
# ============================================================
# This .gitignore is the first line of defense for a PUBLIC repository. It
# excludes local secrets, raw evidence, coursework, transcripts, capture
# files, and machine-identifying local state so they can never be staged
# by accident.
#
# THIS FILE MUST EXIST, COMMITTED, BEFORE THE FIRST COMMIT of this
# repository. If `git init` / the first `git add` happens before this file
# is in place, anything matching the patterns below may already be tracked
# in history — see REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md section 5 ("deleting a file later
# does not remove it from git history").
#
# See REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md before every push — this file prevents accidental
# staging, it does not replace the manual review.
# ============================================================

# ============================================================
# Environment / secrets — never commit real credentials
# ============================================================
.env
.env.*
*.env
.env.local
.env.production

# ============================================================
# Credentials, keys, tokens
# ============================================================
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*
*secret*
*secrets*
*token*
*.p12
*.pfx
service-account*.json
.aws/
.ssh/
*.kdbx

# ============================================================
# Archives — should never ship raw bulk content into a public repo
# ============================================================
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.rar

# ============================================================
# Raw evidence dossiers — summarized in evidence/README.md only,
# the underlying material is never committed
# ============================================================
appendix/
*dossier*
evidence_dossiers/
*_dossiers/

# ============================================================
# Transcripts and data exports — may contain personal/system identifiers
# ============================================================
*transcript*
*conversations*.json
*export*.zip
*.jsonl

# ============================================================
# Course material — graded/licensed content, not for redistribution
# ============================================================
coursework/
*.pka
*.pkt
*.docx
*.pptx

# ============================================================
# Documents that may carry personal data
# ============================================================
*resume*.pdf
*transcript*.pdf

# ============================================================
# Local scratch / build artifacts
# ============================================================
.venv/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
*.tmp

# ============================================================
# Unsanitized screenshots — only redacted images belong in screenshots/
# ============================================================
screenshots/raw/

# ============================================================
# Capture and data files — a security portfolio leaks most easily here.
# Packet captures and browser archives contain real traffic, hostnames,
# cookies, and sometimes credentials in cleartext.
# ============================================================
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.har
*.cap
*.evtx
*.csv
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ============================================================
# Editor / IDE state — leaks local paths and recent-file lists
# ============================================================
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.code-workspace

# ============================================================
# Evidence directory is allowlisted, not blocklisted.
# Only the index and redacted screenshots may be committed; anything
# else placed here is ignored by default so an accidental drop-in
# cannot be staged without a deliberate override.
# ============================================================
evidence/*
!evidence/README.md
!evidence/screenshots/
evidence/screenshots/*
!evidence/screenshots/*.png
!evidence/screenshots/*.jpg
!evidence/screenshots/*.svg
